WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.169
-Trevor, I thought it
would be fun to play

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.303
a brand-new game together.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.039
It is time for "First Try."
Here we go.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.940
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.210
-♪ "First Try" ♪

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.478
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.714
We will both have to
complete the same challenge,

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.983
but we have to do it
on the first try.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.719
Okay, there are no redos
and no second chances.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.387
Whoever completes
the most challenges

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:22.989
on the first try wins.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.323
You ready for this?

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.392
-Wait, wait, wait, wait.
I need to understand the rules.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.627
-Yeah. There's no real --

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.129
-We're doing something
for the first time?

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.196
-Yeah.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.764
-And we have to do it
on the first try?

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.099
-That's correct.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.068
It's something
we've probably done before,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.503
but now the pressure is on.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.272
You have do it just -- You have
one chance to do it right.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.307
-I mean, I'll try,
but, I mean --

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.642
-That's the whole point of --
-Let's see.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:43.843
-That's the whole point
of the game.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.446
-Alright, let's see.
Let's see. Let's do it.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.749
-The first challenge is --
I'm doing it since I'm the host.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:54.320
It's plugging in a USB cord
the correct way without looking.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.554
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
Wait, wait. Without looking?

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:56.823
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.491
So don't look, don't look.
Wait, wait wait, wait.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.659
Let me...

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.827
-Oh, look,
you're flipping it around?

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.061
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Alright, here we go.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:05.331
-Okay, go. Don't look.
Don't look. Don't look.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.466
♪♪

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.169
Ooh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.205
♪♪

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.909
-That's good.
That's a point for me.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.212
That's how fun
and random the game is.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.413
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.414
I feel great.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.649
You have your
USB thing there.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.653
-Yeah, but I don't have a USB --
like, I don't have a hard drive.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.488
I've never done this before.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.190
Someone was like, "Aww."

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.358
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.793
I'm lying.
I've got a USB drive somewhere.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.794
-Here we go.
-Alright.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.197
-Can he do it first try?

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.197
Oh, he can!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.666
♪♪
-Yes! Yes!

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.768
-Alright, alright, alright.
-Yes!

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:44.970
-That is good right there.
Alright, fantastic.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.340
For this next one, okay,
we have to open this book.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.976
You have an advantage here.
-Okay.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.311
-This is your book.
-Alright.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.679
-Paperback. "Born a Crime."

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:54.814
So this is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.049
-Thank you, thank you. Okay.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.585
-Alright, now,
you have to open the book

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.320
to exactly somewhere between

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.956
pages 200 and 250
without looking.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.057
-Yeah, you ready?
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.993
♪♪

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.395
-Oh.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.467
149?!
[ Tuba plays ]

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.968
-217! Yeah, baby!

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.004
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:24.277
Alright, this one...

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.512
This one's hard.
-Can I just say for the record?

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.414
The game I'm having
a fun time with.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.581
I'm enjoying this with you.

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:31.450
That sound effect
is unnecessary.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.819
[ Tuba plays ]

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.387
-Yeah, no, that really -- Yeah.
-That is just like --

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.788
-That's like taking
a bicycle home, isn't it?

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.122
-I mean, that is,
like, a terrible sound.

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:38.924
It doesn't match
what you're trying in life.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.894
[ Tuba plays ]

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.094
-Okay.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.596
-Okay, let's do it.
What are we doing here?

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.465
-This next round, we're going to
have to flip the water bottle

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.400
and have it
land straight up on the desk.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.434
Since you're my guest,
you go first.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.937
-Oh, man, this is -- No!

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.971
Okay, wait.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.673
I used to remember
how to do this.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.841
Wait. Alright, hold on, hold on.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.877
♪♪

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.647
The keyboard --
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:02.648
The keyboard was there.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.283
We'll move the keyboard.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.385
I think what
you're trying to do is this.

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.855
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.855
-There's no way.

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:11.925
No.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.328
[ Tuba plays ]

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.129
-Alright, wait, wait.
This one, let's try to --

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.331
-[ Laughs ]
-Let's just try to do it again.

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:20.333
Whoever can do it
the first time.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.467
-Okay.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.568
-We're changing the rules
a little bit here.

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.671
-Alright. I'll try again.
I'll try again.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.038
So, when you were standing up,
was that easier?

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:27.773
-That was easier.
I liked standing up.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.108
[ Groans ]

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.610
[ Tuba plays ]

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:37.049
-We're going to fight.
♪♪

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.717
No. No.
[ Tuba plays ]

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:41.654
-Okay, I'm just gonna keep
flipping this thing.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.388
I'm just going to
keep flipping this bottle.

00:03:43.388 --> 00:03:45.058
I'm not going to fail.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.694
-There's a slide there.
-Almost, almost.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.730
-Oh, God. Way off. Let me get...

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.765
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:01.341
That's what I'm talking
about right there.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.376
Oh, that's how you
do it right there.

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:07.246
Come on, now!

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.714
-I'm going to have nightmares
about that sound.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.449
-I know.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.818
-Oh, man.
-He's exhausted. Alright.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:16.222
Do we have time for one more
first try, first time?

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.624
-Alright.
-That was amazing right there.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.058
We could have
ended it right there,

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.059
and that would have
been perfect.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.460
But, instead, this one is ---

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.562
-Eat the popcorn without
it getting stuck in your teeth.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.130
-No.
-Oh.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.533
-Toss it up in the air
and then catch it in your mouth.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.269
-Oh, yeah, no.
I think I can do that first try.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.502
-I think I can do
that first try. Ready?

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:31.937
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:34.173
♪♪

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:37.510
Yeah, that wasn't good bite.
Ready?

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.345
-Wait, wait, wait.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.547
-Yeah, a little breeze.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.348
-A little breeze.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.348 --> 00:04:45.951
Here we go. 1, 2, 3...

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.987
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.789
-He's the winner.
That's the champ right there!

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:51.790
-The wind.
-Trevor Noah!

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:52.792
-The wind is blowing.

